testing:
UasSort.Core.Tests (xUnit) holds nearly all tests and needs no real disk. Planning is pure and takes records, and I/O goes through IFileOps with an in-memory FakeFileOps.
1. FileClassifier table tests: every row of the card-layout classification table, including DJI_002_A01, 100MEDIA, PANORAMA/001_0087, .DJI_…MP4.trinf, *.LRF, *.SRT, MISC, a JPG that shares an MP4 base name, and .MOV (Unknown).
2. Mp4Probe: a synthetic MP4 builder in the test project, ported from spikes/djmd/synth_test.py. Cases:
   - moov first and moov last;
   - 64-bit mdat and co64;
   - 3 samples per chunk with 2 stsd entries, djmd second;
   - sample 0 zeroed (fix taken from the last sample);
   - GPS zeroed everywhere (null);
   - no moov (HasMoov = false).
   Optional golden tests, run when UASSORT_GOLDEN points at local files: Zachar Bay _0128 gives 57.5504420579265, -153.738972972093 and mvhd 2026-09-27T18:06:27Z; Anvil _0001 gives 64.5626761883622. Plus StillProbe on PANO_0001.DNG: 57.799648, -152.390180, DTO 2026-05-25 09:30:28.
3. DroneClock/TimeResolver, with a fake ISiteZone:
   - midnight: 20260726035000 is local 7/25;
   - a Hawaii clip at 09:30Z gets local date 2/28;
   - DST: an October −4 sample and a November −5 sample, and a November DNG takes −5;
   - no MP4 on the card falls back to the setting;
   - Autel floating time;
   - Etc/* falls back to the PC zone.
   One Windows-only test uses the real GeoTimeZone for Anchorage, Nome, New_York and Honolulu.
4. Clusterer and FolderDecider scenarios, ported from spikes/grouping/test_grouping.py, dropping the session and photo-attach cases, which this design removes:
   - Council Road (7/25) vs Anvil Mountain (7/26), 53 km apart: 2 groups;
   - Kodiak-style 4 consecutive days: 1 group;
   - Zachar Bay then Kodiak town on the same day: 2 groups;
   - A-B-A on one day: 3 groups;
   - Newport 4.8 km apart and Nome 12 km apart: 1 group each;
   - R = 60 merges and R = 25 splits;
   - 7/31→8/2 lands under 2026-07; 12/31→1/1 lands under 2026-12;
   - an existing-folder hard boundary;
   - append today, both high and medium confidence;
   - next day near → Append; next day far or unknown → NewFolder;
   - a date before a folder's name date never appends;
   - Makaha legacy depth → Append to 2022\\2022-03-27 Makaha Valley;
   - a centroid across the antimeridian.
5. Replay fixture: a checked-in JSON of the library listing (relative path, size, mtime only) plus the GPS from spikes/djmd/calibration.json and spikes/grouping/more_gps.json. It must give 8 groups equal to the 8 user folders, plus scenarios A–E. I already confirmed these hold with this design's simplified rules, in Python (spikes/minimal-arch/minimal_cluster.py and minimal_decide.py):
   - 8 of 8 folders; R ok for 12.5–53 km; G ok for 1–11 days;
   - B: NewFolder 2026/2026-09/2026-09-27 (13 clips);
   - C: Append to 2026-09-27 Zachar Bay (4 new);
   - D and E: NewFolder 2026-07-26 (21 clips).
6. Newness:
   - same name with a 7 MiB size is a Conflict;
   - a ledger hit is Imported;
   - a photo after the watermark is New;
   - a photo on a new-video day is New;
   - a photo-only day before the watermark is ProbablyImported;
   - set 001_0087 matching the library is Imported; 001_0112 with the same PANO names is New, with a collision suffix.
7. FolderNamer.Clean: 'Newport, RI' is kept; ' A/B: \"test\"? ' becomes 'A B test'; 'Nome Rd...' becomes 'Nome Rd'.
8. GuardedFileOps rules: OpenRead under either root throws, except *.uas-sort.tmp; any write under the card root throws; DeleteTemp on a non-tmp file throws.
9. CopyEngine with FakeFileOps:
   - happy path, with the ledger written after verification;
   - AlreadyThere;
   - different size gives Failed;
   - an injected hash mismatch retries, then fails;
   - cancel removes the tmp;
   - an insufficient free-space preflight blocks the run.
   One Windows integration test in %TEMP%\\uas-sort-test covers unbuffered verify, timestamp preservation and move-without-overwrite, and cleans up after itself.
Manual acceptance: the first real run uses settings roots pointed at scratch folders (C:\\Temp\\uas-sort-test\\videos and \\photos). Compare the result with the plan, then switch to the real roots.

components.interface:
interface ISourceVolume {   // read-only by construction: no write, rename or delete members
  VolumeIdentity Identity { get; }                  // root, VolumeSerial, Label, FileSystem, Fingerprint (xxh64 of sorted relPath|size)
  IEnumerable<SourceEntry> Enumerate(CancellationToken ct);   // RelPath, Size, LastWriteUtc, RawAttributes
  SourceEntry? Stat(string relPath);
  Stream OpenRead(string relPath, ReadPattern p);   // FileAccess.Read, FileShare.Read; RandomAccess or SequentialScan
}
interface ILibraryLister {  // there is NO Open method: library files are never read
  LibrarySnapshot List(RootSpec root, CancellationToken ct);  // entries: RelPath, Name, Size, LastWriteUtc, RawAttributes, IsCloudOnly
}
interface IDestinationFs {
  DestStat? Stat(string path);
  IReadOnlyList<string> EnsureDirectory(string path);        // returns the directories it actually created
  Stream CreateTemp(string tmpPath, long preallocate);        // FileMode.CreateNew only
  void FlushDurable(Stream s);                                // Flush(flushToDisk: true)
  void SetTimes(string tmpPath, DateTime creationUtc, DateTime writeUtc);
  CommitResult RenameNoReplace(string tmp, string final);     // MoveFileEx with WRITE_THROUGH, never REPLACE_EXISTING; returns TargetExists instead of throwing
  Stream OpenReadUnbuffered(string path);                     // FILE_FLAG_NO_BUFFERING, aligned buffers; refuses cloud-only files
  void DeleteOwnTemp(string tmpPath);                         // throws unless the name matches *.{sessionTag}.uas-sort.tmp
  bool TryRemoveOwnEmptyDirectory(string path);               // only directories the journal says this session created
  long FreeBytes(string root);
  VolumeIdentity VolumeOf(string path);
}

IsCloudOnly means (attributes & (0x400000 | 0x40000 | 0x1000)) != 0.

