components.responsibility:
Every user edit is a typed command that turns one Plan into another. Undo and redo work because the editor keeps a stack of Plan snapshots, which are immutable and structurally shared. Commands store ItemIds, so a draft can be replayed onto a fresh scan of the same card. Invariants that always hold:
- every video belongs to exactly one group;
- there are no empty groups;
- photo membership is always derived by AttachPhotos, never edited;
- structural edits apply to video groups only.

