components.responsibility:
Reads only the bytes it needs from card files.

**Mp4Probe** (port of spike B's djmd_gps.py) walks the MP4 structure lazily. It never reads mdat and never reads moov whole. It returns:
- the mvhd creation time as UTC (Autel files are handled as floating local time);
- whether moov is present;
- the first GPS fix from djmd, probing samples 0-9, then powers of two, then the last sample, plus the last fix;
- the power-on session and the drone serial;
- the byte ranges of the tnal (160x90) and covr (960x540) thumbnails.
- **Fallback for truncated clips:** when moov is missing, read the mdat head at offset 512.

**StillProbe** uses MetadataExtractor to read:
- DateTimeOriginal (from the directory that actually contains it, not the first sub-IFD);
- GPS and the camera model;
- the byte ranges of the IFD0 JPEG thumbnail and the SubIFD1 JPEG preview.

**MetadataHarvester** schedules the work:
- videos first, because they define the groups;
- at most 2 files read in parallel, since SD cards are serial devices;
- progress is streamed so the UI can fill in as it goes.

